{
 "result": "Built csvsum.py: reads all of stdin, skips the header, splits each line on the first two commas, accumulates float val per cat in a dict keyed by bytes, then writes 'cat,sum' with %.2f sorted by cat. Verified with test_csvsum.py (header-only input, basic sums, negatives producing 0.00, rounding case, and a 1000-row randomized 17-category case where output matched an independently computed expected string byte-for-byte \u2014 all OK). Performance: on a generated 2,000,001-line file (2M rows, 8 categories) it runs in 0.73s real via /usr/bin/time, printing alpha..theta with correct sums (e.g. alpha,1249990000.00). A Kahan-compensated variant was probed in kahan.py for numerical drift, but the naive float dict accumulation was kept since it is fast and matched expected sums on the test corpus.",
